---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';

// Rewritten for the static site: no forms, no newsletter, no accounts, no
// cookies, no Google Analytics. Only Vercel (hosting) and Matomo (cookieless,
// IP-anonymised analytics) are mentioned, because they are the only services used.
const updated = '24 November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How the nZEBRA website handles data. The site sets no cookies, runs no trackers that identify you, and collects no personal data through forms."
>
  <div class="news-wrap">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Header variant="light" />
      <div class="uui-page-padding-3">
        <div class="uui-container-large-3">
          <div class="uui-padding-vertical-xhuge-5">
            <div class="uui-max-width-large-3">
              <h1 class="uui-heading-large">Privacy policy</h1>
              <div class="uui-space-small-3"></div>
              <article class="uui-text-rich-text w-richtext">
                <p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>

                <h3>About this website</h3>
                <p>
                  This website (<a href="https://nzebra.eu">www.nzebra.eu</a>) presents the work of
                  the nZEBRA project, an initiative co-funded by the European Union under the
                  Erasmus+ programme. It is an information-only website: it has no accounts, no
                  login, no contact forms and no newsletter sign-up.
                </p>

                <h3>What data we collect</h3>
                <p>
                  We do not ask you for any personal data on this website, and there are no forms to
                  submit it through. We do not set any cookies.
                </p>
                <p>
                  As with any website, our hosting provider automatically processes basic technical
                  information needed to deliver pages to you (such as your IP address and browser
                  type) in its server logs. We also measure anonymous, aggregate usage statistics as
                  described below.
                </p>

                <h3>Hosting</h3>
                <p>
                  The website is hosted by Vercel. Vercel processes the technical request data
                  described above on our behalf in order to serve the site and protect it against
                  abuse. See Vercel’s privacy notice at
                  <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy</a>.
                </p>

                <h3>Analytics</h3>
                <p>
                  To understand which pages are useful, we use Matomo in a privacy-friendly
                  configuration. Matomo:
                </p>
                <ul>
                  <li>does not set any cookies and does not track you across websites;</li>
                  <li>anonymises your IP address, so you are not personally identified;</li>
                  <li>produces only aggregate statistics (such as page views and referring sites).</li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                  Because the data is anonymous and no cookies are used, this analytics does not
                  require a consent banner.
                </p>

                <h3>Documents</h3>
                <p>
                  Course materials and project documents (PDF and Office files) are served directly
                  from this website. Downloading them does not require you to provide any
                  information.
                </p>

                <h3>External links</h3>
                <p>
                  Some pages link to external websites (for example partner institutions or EU
                  resources). Those sites have their own privacy policies, which we do not control.
                </p>

                <h3>Your data protection rights</h3>
                <p>
                  Under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) you have rights of access,
                  rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and portability regarding your
                  personal data. Because this website does not collect personal data that identifies
                  you, we normally hold nothing to act on — but you can contact us at any time with a
                  request or question.
                </p>

                <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
                <p>
                  We may update this policy if the services behind the website change. The date at
                  the top shows when it was last revised.
                </p>

                <h3>How to contact us</h3>
                <p>
                  For any question about this policy or your data, email
                  <a href="mailto:hello@threeoclock.eu">hello@threeoclock.eu</a>.
                </p>

                <h3>Supervisory authority</h3>
                <p>
                  If you believe your data protection rights have not been respected, you have the
                  right to lodge a complaint with your national data protection authority.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
